# The voice pack IS tracked: GitHub Pages serves the site out of the repo, so a
# repo without the mp3s hosts an app that quietly falls back to the device voice.
# (Plain git, not LFS — LFS's free tier caps at 1 GB/month of bandwidth, which is
# only ~60 first installs of a 15 MB pack. Pages' own 100 GB/month is the gentler
# limit.) Re-generate with `npm run voices`; build-site.py fails loudly if a clip
# promised by audio/manifest.json is missing.
# audio/

# Generated art: the renders and the rejects stay out of the repo, the promoted
# covers do not — Pages serves the site out of this repo, so a cover the app
# points at has to be here. tools/make-story-art.py --promote writes webp only.
images/_candidates/
images/**/*.png
images/**/*.jpg
!images/books/*.webp

# generated by tools/build-portable.py for file:// only — the hosted site
# must never ship these, a baked-in index is how silent books get published
audio/pack-index.js
audio/books/pack-index.js
